 td_ex_attendees: "Me (PM), Sarah (Eng Lead), Marcus (Design), Priya (CEO)",
 td_ex_context: "Weekly product review — we were supposed to align on the v2 launch scope. Sarah's been pushing to cut the analytics dashboard, Priya wants it in.",
 td_ex_transcript: "Priya: OK let's start with where we are on v2. Sarah, what's the engineering picture?\n\nSarah: Honestly, tight. The core flows are in good shape — onboarding redesign is shipping next week, the new pricing page is in QA. But the analytics dashboard is going to slip. We're looking at maybe three more weeks if we don't cut scope.\n\nPriya: Three weeks past launch?\n\nSarah: Yeah. The aggregation queries are slower than we thought, and we found a security issue with the way we were exposing customer-level data.\n\nMarcus: Could we ship a simpler version? Just top-line metrics, no drill-down?\n\nSarah: Maybe. That's like a week, not three.\n\nPriya: I'd rather have something at launch than nothing. Customers we've previewed it with — that's literally what they asked about first.\n\nMe: I think we go with Marcus's suggestion. Ship the v1 dashboard, full version in a fast-follow. I can write up what's in scope by end of day.\n\nPriya: Agreed. Sarah, comfortable with that?\n\nSarah: Yeah, that's doable. I'll have a real estimate tomorrow.\n\nPriya: Great. Marcus — any blockers on design?\n\nMarcus: All green. Patterns are reusable from the existing reporting view.",
